# ── KEY MATERIAL. Nothing here may ever be committed. ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A launch record holds the MINT'S SECRET KEY — it has to, because re-sending with the same
# mint is a retry and re-sending with a new one is a second token. A Solana CLI keypair file
# holds the launch wallet's secret key outright. `git add -A` after a launch would publish
# either one to GitHub, where it is scraped in minutes.
#
# These patterns are a backstop, NOT the plan. The plan is that keys live outside the
# repository entirely — see LAUNCH.md, which puts them in ~/.snooze — because a pattern only
# catches the filenames somebody thought of, and `solana-keygen grind` writes a file named
# after an address nobody can predict.
launch-*.json
launch.json
id.json
mint-*.json
*keypair*.json
*.keypair
.snooze/

# ── ordinary junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vercel
node_modules/
